# Build artefacts
/bin/
/dist/
/pql
/pql.exe

# Test, coverage, profile output
*.test
*.out
*.prof
*.pprof
coverage.*
/tmp/

# Go module + workspace artefacts (we don't vendor; we don't use workspaces)
/vendor/
/go.work
/go.work.sum

# pql's own per-vault state. The project itself isn't a vault, but if
# anyone runs pql against the repo root (testing, dogfooding), .pql/
# lands here. Mirror what `pql init` writes to consumers' .gitignore:
# ignore everything except the planning snapshot and the replication
# changelog (D-15: per-table monthly SQL files that get committed and
# shared between replicas). .pql/hooks/ is per-clone state (T-28) —
# `pql init` plants it locally on every clone with the binary path
# baked in; tracking would produce per-developer drift.
.pql/*
!.pql/changelog/

# clean-house skill local working state (run history + skip ledger).
# Per-clone, not shared — like the skip ledger of a linter cache.
governance/decisions/.clean-house-state.md

# SQLite index files should never land here, but defensive
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db

# Secrets
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Claude Code user-specific settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# pql shims planted by `pql init` into git's hooks dir (the dir
# `core.hooksPath` points at — `.githooks/` here). Each shim bridges
# git's hooks dir to the matching body in `.pql/hooks/`. Both the shim
# and the body are per-clone state, replanted on every `pql init`
# (see T-28 / T-52): the bodies bake a per-developer absolute pql path,
# and — the load-bearing reason — a contributor who doesn't use pql (or
# clide) must be able to clone and work in this repo without pql's hook
# machinery landing in their tree. `pre-push` is NOT listed here: it's
# the project's own `make pre-push` CI gate, not a pql-tool shim, and is
# tracked deliberately.
.githooks/pre-commit
.githooks/post-merge
.githooks/post-checkout
.githooks/post-rewrite
